<title>DENMARK: Denmark upwardly revises c/a for 1996.</title>
<headline>Denmark upwardly revises c/a for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's National Statistics Office on Wednesday said it revised upward its full year 1996 current account surplus figures to 16.7 billion crowns, from a previously published 14.8 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The office attributed the adjustment to auditing procedures.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
